  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000. The project has since secured a $2M budget approved by the executive board. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the prototype for secure file sharing, which was tested ahead of schedule. The project is entering the development phase under lead developer Omar Jensen, following the design phase. Strategic partnerships are being explored and established with TechInnovate to leverage AI technology. The team has expanded to include Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November, and a celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
